So now for the business at hand.

244
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,897
Tell me who your user
is and where he lives.

245
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:32,804
Do that and I'll spare your life,
which is more than you deserve.

246
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:34,250
Interesting.

247
00:13:34,333 --> 00:13:36,360
If I tell you, you'll spare me, huh?

248
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:38,480
You're surprisingly composed.

249
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:43,078
I was positive your bowels would be
burning with vengeful fury by now!

250
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:48,297
To be honest, I'm secretly hoping you
won't give me the info on your user.

251
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:51,597
I mentioned to scrape you away,
you glow-in-the-dark shithead.

252
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:52,920
So give me a reason.

253
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,400
There's the real you!

254
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,240
Thinking you can kill me?

255
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,180
With that sluggish right hand.

256
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,054
I don't know if I should laugh or yawn,

257
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:06,737
but either way you won't be
putting out my lights today.

258
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:07,720
You bastard!

259
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:10,020
I'll end you!

260
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:12,937
And I'll make sure you realize
how pathetic your stand

261
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:16,100
is when compared to the
marvel that is Chili Pepper!

262
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:29,180
Now do you finally understand how slow
you are? Okuyasu! Okuyasu! Not good.

263
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:30,860
Here comes Jotaro.

264
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,817
I can't stick around much longer.

265
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:33,730
Huh?

266
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,460
How'd he get behind me?

267
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,097
You're right about me being slow,
and I may have missed the mark,

268
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:43,617
but I swiped away space, which
gives me the ability to teleport.

269
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,380
Did you forget about that?

270
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,500
How do you like that?

271
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,340
You big-nosed freak!

272
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:08,837
I might be wrong, but it seems
like you're not as fast as before.

273
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:12,257
Do you think someone as slow as
you can slip by my next attack?

274
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:13,222
Look, you guys.

275
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,617
Chili Pepper's electric charge is fading.

276
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:17,597
He's getting weaker and
weaker by the second.

277
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,457
His stand must be running out of power.

278
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:20,677
Well, would you look at that.

279
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:21,878
He actually did it.

280
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,800
Okuyasu, leave him alive.

281
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,457
We'll handle him once we get over there.

282
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:26,700
You've already won.

283
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,637
Now our primary focus needs to be getting

284
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:31,157
him to tell us where
the bow and arrow are.

285
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,917
You're right about one thing.

286
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,640
My energy is fading.

287
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:37,597
Your stand may be as slow as molasses,

288
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:41,092
but the ferocity of his attack
is downright bone-chilling.

289
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:46,809
That being said, don't you want to finish
off your brother's killer for good?

290
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:49,400
Try using your head for a moment.

291
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:53,248
How can you be certain I'm not
simply pretending to be frail?

292
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,710
Okuyasu...

293
00:15:54,793 --> 00:15:55,623
What?

294
00:15:55,706 --> 00:15:59,140
Who's to say I'm not luring Jotaro in
close so I can cleave off his head?

295
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,720
Quit spouting bullshit!

296
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:02,120
Fine by me.

297
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,360
So what'll it be?

298
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:05,337
Will you do away with me now?

299
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:07,880
Or wait for me to get the drop on Jotaro?

300
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,380
You bastard.

301
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,100
Hold on a minute.

302
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:18,057
If you were really up to something
shady, why would you tell me your plan?

303
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:21,317
Had he just kept his beak shut, he
could have easily played us all.

304
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:25,277
He would have been in the perfect
position to take me and Jotaro out.

305
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:26,740
And if that's the case,

306
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,397
since he basically told me
nothing's wrong with him,

307
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:32,177
the chances of him attacking
me are practically zero.

308
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:34,220
At least I think they are.

309
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,937
Are you trying to say you
want me to kill you after all?

310
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:40,491
I'll let you come to your own conclusions.

311
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,960
This is so confusing!

312
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:44,693
Is he on his last legs?

313
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,277
Or is he lying through his
beak waiting to attack?

314
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,620
Which one is it?

315
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:52,898
What's your answer?

316
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:54,577
Are you gonna do it or not?

317
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:59,057
If this asshole isn't really injured,
I have to kill him right here and now.

318
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,728
But is that the right move?

319
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:03,135
He could have something up his sleeve.

320
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:07,700
Shit! Should I?

321
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:10,960
Okuyasu, I better get over there.

322
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:13,180
Last chance.

323
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,148
Make up your mind, Okuyasu.

324
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,600
The hell with it!

325
00:17:24,940 --> 00:17:27,857
I'm putting an end to this
nightmare once and for all!

326
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:29,000
It's time to die!

327
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:30,810
Okuyasu!

328
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:33,657
Don't even think about
trying to stop me, Jotaro!

329
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:34,920
He killed my bro!

330
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,717
That means he has to
pay the ultimate price!

331
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:40,437
That's the only truth
that matters right now!

332
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:43,140
And my heart has shown
me what I need to do!

333
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:46,462
Now eat, shit, and die,
you glorified nightlight!

334
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:53,780
Well, that's just great.

335
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:57,137
Finding the bow and arrow is going
to be a real pain in the ass now.

336
00:17:57,220 --> 00:17:59,749
At least he settled
things with that freak.

337
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:00,930
Hang on.

338
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:02,097
Something doesn't feel right.

339
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:03,474
We need to be careful.

340
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,880
My gut's telling me Chili
Pepper is still a threat.

341
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,485
Underground electrical cables?

342
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,680
That bastard!

343
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:18,200
He faked all that so I'd expose them!

344
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,520
Not quite.

345
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:22,320
I really was fading.

346
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,560
That motorcycle battery
only holds 12 volts.

347
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:28,799
A few moments longer and I
would have been done for!

348
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:34,540
I must thank you for reviving me!

349
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,420
Poor simple-minded Okuyasu.

350
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:42,957
If only you'd been a good boy and
controlled yourself as Totoro instructed,

351
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:45,452
I would have faded away with the battery.

352
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:50,380
I know the location of every electrical
line running through this town.

353
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:53,560
My original plan was to
escape into those cables,

354
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:56,357
but they were too far
away from the motorcycle.

355
00:18:56,440 --> 00:19:00,381
And in the state I was in, digging
them up was out of the question.

356
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:02,260
Why won't you die?

357
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,660
He's faster than before.

358
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,391
With this much electricity at my disposal,

359
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:09,617
I have more than enough
power to challenge?

360
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:11,288
your lackluster right hand.

361
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,470
Ah!

362
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:26,870
Okuyasu!

363
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,897
I seem to remember your
brother Keicho saying

364
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:38,980
something about you never
failing to hold him back.

365
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:41,200
Oh, how right he was.

366
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:43,337
Your soul is underdeveloped.

367
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:44,340
Ah-ha-ha!

368
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:48,597
Revenge was never going to be within
your reach, you cocksure ignoramus!

369
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,380
So long, Jotaro and Josuke.

370
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:51,642
I'm taking off!

371
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:54,557
But not before I find that
old coot Joseph Joestar?

372
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,517
And see to it that he
shares the same fate!

373
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:58,718
as the lamentable Nijimura brothers!

374
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:00,600
To the victor go the spoils!

375
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:02,040
Okuyasu, no!

376
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,940
He pulled him into the cables!

377
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:15,340
Okuyasu! Okuyasu!

378
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:17,220
Good grief.

379
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:20,237
To think we were that close
and he still got away.

380
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:22,500
That stand was absolutely terrifying.

381
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:25,897
How do you even begin to fight
a remote stand with boundless

382
00:20:25,980 --> 00:20:27,397
power to tap into every
electrical company within reach?

383
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,937
What the hell are you guys talking about?!

384
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:30,297
Okuyasu was...

385
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:34,657
He was murdered in cold blood and you're
rambling about how strong the enemy was?!

386
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:36,280
Oh yeah, you're right.

387
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,245
We should check up on Okuyasu.

388
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:39,170
Leave it to me.

389
00:20:39,253 --> 00:20:41,400
There's one consolation in all this.

390
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:45,136
He must have had a guardian
angel looking out for him.

391
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:46,257
Weird as it sounds,

392
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:49,437
his right arm getting chopped off was
the best thing that could have happened.

393
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:50,350
Huh?

394
00:20:50,433 --> 00:20:51,629
Let's go, Shining Diamond!

395
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:56,497
You don't have to worry,
so dry those tears, Koichi.

396
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:59,168
Once I fix his arm, his
body will come back.

397
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,360
What the hell?

398
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:04,960
All right!

399
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:07,840
I thought we lost you for good, Okuyasu!

400
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,070
Shit!

401
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:13,937
I... I...

402
00:21:14,020 --> 00:21:16,820
I was totally outclassed by that bastard!

403
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:25,335
It's not about revenge, and
we can't focus on setbacks.

404
00:21:26,340 --> 00:21:27,300
Joseph Joestar.

405
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:30,040
He's the priority here. He needs us.

406
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:31,560
I know it's tough,

407
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:35,177
but that's how we're gonna beat
Chili Pepper and get true justice.

408
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:37,260
You have to do this for our town.

409
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:41,837
And if that isn't enough, then do it
for all the people you care about.

410
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:44,979
I might be stating the
obvious, but this isn't good.

411
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:47,077
Guess I was taking this too lightly.

412
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:50,807
Yeah, we have to reach the old
man's boat before Chili Pepper.

413
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:52,037
Let's head to the port.

414
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:54,877
How can you be so nonchalant
at a time like this?

415
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:57,517
Look at Okuyasu, he's
still in shock over here.

416
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,780
We can get to the port
faster this way. Sounds good.

417
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:02,840
Would you guys wait for us?

418
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:04,877
There's no way around it, bro.

419
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:08,489
Mario, in order to beat Chili
Pepper, I have to surpass you.

420
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:14,910
Mr.

421
00:22:14,993 --> 00:22:18,426
Joestar, we'll be arriving at
the Port of Mario any moment now.

422
00:23:05,713 --> 00:23:07,277
In the face of the humic
and of all that I need

423
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,257
to I want to come stand
a little bit closer.

424
00:23:10,340 --> 00:23:16,997
Breathe in and get a bit higher you'll
never know what hit you when I get to you.

425
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:20,357
Oh I want you I don't know if I

426
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:24,337
need you but oh I gotta find you.

427
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:29,417
Oh I want you I don't know if I

428
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:33,380
need you but oh I gotta find you.

429
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:38,737
Breakdown, breakdown.

430
00:23:38,820 --> 00:23:41,400
Breakdown, breakdown.
